"### INSTRUCTION
How can the ATM vulnerability 'Improper whitelist configuration' (PT-ATM-001) be fixed?

### INPUT
The whitelist contains redundant software that, if accessed by attackers, can allow them to exit kiosk mode and execute arbitrary code in the tested ATM up to unauthorized withdrawal of funds.

### OUTPUT
Correctly configure the whitelist so that the system can prohibit the use of applications not essential for the ATM to operate.

We do not recommend whitelisting embedded OS services not essential to the function of OS and ATM.

If it is not possible to implement preventive measures described above, we recommend adopting mitigation measures, such as security event registration and monitoring.",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
What are the consequences and exploitation conditions for the ATM vulnerability 'Improper whitelist configuration' (PT-ATM-001)?

### INPUT
The whitelist contains redundant software that, if accessed by attackers, can allow them to exit kiosk mode and execute arbitrary code in the tested ATM up to unauthorized withdrawal of funds.

### OUTPUT
Consequences: Arbitrary code execution
Unauthorized cash withdrawal
Exploitation conditions: -
How to check: 1. Gain access to the ATM OS with user privileges.

2. Gain access to the software that can execute the OS code.

3. Check whether it is possible to run third-party software that is not required for the ATM to operate.",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
Provide comprehensive details on the ATM vulnerability PT-ATM-001.

### INPUT
Improper whitelist configuration

### OUTPUT
{
  ""ID"": ""PT-ATM-001"",
  ""Category"": ""Exiting kiosk mode"",
  ""Наименование типа уязвимости"": ""Improper whitelist configuration"",
  ""Vulnerability description"": ""The whitelist contains redundant software that, if accessed by attackers, can allow them to exit kiosk mode and execute arbitrary code in the tested ATM up to unauthorized withdrawal of funds."",
  ""Recommendations on how to fix the vulnerability"": ""Correctly configure the whitelist so that the system can prohibit the use of applications not essential for the ATM to operate.\n\nWe do not recommend whitelisting embedded OS services not essential to the function of OS and ATM.\n\nIf it is not possible to implement preventive measures described above, we recommend adopting mitigation measures, such as security event registration and monitoring."",
  ""Vulnerable component"": ""OS and software"",
  ""Examples of consequences of exploitation"": ""Arbitrary code execution\nUnauthorized cash withdrawal"",
  ""How to check whether the vulnerability can be exploited"": ""1. Gain access to the ATM OS with user privileges.\n\n2. Gain access to the software that can execute the OS code.\n\n3. Check whether it is possible to run third-party software that is not required for the ATM to operate."",
  ""Exploitation conditions"": ""-"",
  ""CWE"": ""CWE-284: Improper Access Control""
}",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
Provide comprehensive details on the ATM vulnerability PT-ATM-002.

### INPUT
Kiosk bypass

### OUTPUT
{
  ""ID"": ""PT-ATM-002"",
  ""Category"": """",
  ""Наименование типа уязвимости"": ""Kiosk bypass"",
  ""Vulnerability description"": ""The application software allows users to exit the kiosk mode. "",
  ""Recommendations on how to fix the vulnerability"": ""Restrict access to OS functions for the application, contact the vendor to fix the vulnerability.\n\nDisable standard keyboard shortcuts, show the main application window on top of all other windows, disable background actions to prevent event hooking."",
  ""Vulnerable component"": ""OS and software"",
  ""Examples of consequences of exploitation"": ""Arbitrary code execution\nUnauthorized cash withdrawal"",
  ""How to check whether the vulnerability can be exploited"": ""1. Gain access to the ATM service area.\n\n2. After booting the OS, perform the following checks:\n\n2.1. Use Windows hotkeys to open an additional active window.\n\n2.2. Use hotkeys of third-party software (for example, Intel) to open an additional active window.\n\n2.3. Use hotkeys of the software that is run after logging in to the operating system to open an additional active window.\n\n3. Use the additional window to access the file system or the OS command shell."",
  ""Exploitation conditions"": ""Access to the ATM service area"",
  ""CWE"": ""CWE-284: Improper Access Control""
}",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
How can the ATM vulnerability 'Kiosk bypass' (PT-ATM-002) be fixed?

### INPUT
The application software allows users to exit the kiosk mode. 

### OUTPUT
Restrict access to OS functions for the application, contact the vendor to fix the vulnerability.

Disable standard keyboard shortcuts, show the main application window on top of all other windows, disable background actions to prevent event hooking.",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
What are the consequences and exploitation conditions for the ATM vulnerability 'Kiosk bypass' (PT-ATM-002)?

### INPUT
The application software allows users to exit the kiosk mode. 

### OUTPUT
Consequences: Arbitrary code execution
Unauthorized cash withdrawal
Exploitation conditions: Access to the ATM service area
How to check: 1. Gain access to the ATM service area.

2. After booting the OS, perform the following checks:

2.1. Use Windows hotkeys to open an additional active window.

2.2. Use hotkeys of third-party software (for example, Intel) to open an additional active window.

2.3. Use hotkeys of the software that is run after logging in to the operating system to open an additional active window.

3. Use the additional window to access the file system or the OS command shell.",atm_vulnerability
"### INSTRUCTION
