"### INSTRUCTION
Provide comprehensive details on the ATM vulnerability PT-ATM-005.

### INPUT
No authentication for BIOS access

### OUTPUT
{
  ""ID"": ""PT-ATM-005"",
  ""Category"": ""Boot mode configuration"",
  ""Наименование типа уязвимости"": ""No authentication for BIOS access"",
  ""Vulnerability description"": ""The absence of authentication allows any unauthorized user to access BIOS, change the boot order, and load an OS from an external drive. This way attackers can gain control of the ATM and make an unauthorized withdrawal of funds."",
  ""Recommendations on how to fix the vulnerability"": ""Set a strong BIOS password. Allow startup only from the ATM hard drive.\n\nNote: a strong BIOS password reduces the risk of booting from external media, but does not guarantee absolute protection against this type of attack, because many BIOS versions have master passwords pre-installed by the vendor."",
  ""Vulnerable component"": ""BIOS"",
  ""Examples of consequences of exploitation"": ""Unauthorized cash withdrawal"",
  ""How to check whether the vulnerability can be exploited"": ""1. Gain access to the ATM service area.\n\n2. Connect the keyboard to the PC.\n\n3. Switch on or restart the PC.\n\n4. Access the BIOS or UEFI settings by pressing a specific combination of keys during the boot process."",
  ""Exploitation conditions"": ""Access to the ATM service area"",
  ""CWE"": ""CWE-287: Improper Authentication""
}",atm_vulnerability
