What are the consequences and exploitation conditions for the ATM vulnerability 'Use of insecure (open) protocols' (PT-ATM-405)?

### INPUT
Open protocols are used in the ATM. Data is transferred without encryption and can be easily intercepted by an attacker listening to the network. As a result, sensitive information may be intercepted.

### OUTPUT
Consequences: Obtaining confidential data
Exploitation conditions: Constant: access to the ATM network traffic
How to check: 1. Obtain access to network traffic transferred between the ATM and the processing center.

